From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: apple,s8000-mca: Add the S5L8960X MCA

The A7's MCAs (Apple's mca,s5l8960x, mca-version 1) are the T7001's
version 1 block. On the iPad Air, MCA0 is a playback I2S link to the
CS42L81 codec, which provides the bit and frame clocks, as on the A9:
add apple,s5l8960x-mca, without a bitclock NCO.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml        | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
index fcadf6dbc..917689968 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple T7001/S8000/T8010 MCA I2S controller
+title: Apple S5L8960X/T7001/S8000/T8010 MCA I2S controller
 
 maintainers:
   - Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
@@ -21,7 +21,10 @@ description: |
   the link setup iOS programs into it. The T7001 (A8X) MCA is the older
   "mca-version 1" register layout with the same fields: apple,t7001-mca is
   the playback-only speaker link (TDM) of the iPad Air 2, clocked from an AP
-  NCO channel running at twice the bit clock.
+  NCO channel running at twice the bit clock. The S5L8960X (A7) MCA is
+  version 1 as well: apple,s5l8960x-mca is the playback-only I2S link of the
+  iPad Air to its codec, which provides the bit and frame clocks as on the
+  A9.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: dai-common.yaml#
@@ -49,6 +52,7 @@ allOf:
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - apple,s5l8960x-mca
       - apple,s8000-mca
       - apple,t7001-mca
       - apple,t8010-mca
-- 
2.56.0

